# Responsive UI

Any UI change or addition must work on **mobile, tablet, laptop, and desktop**.

Do not ship layouts that only look correct on a large monitor.

- Prefer stacking or wrapping over fixed multi-column rows when space is tight.
- Size to the available panel when a viewport media query is not enough (container queries are fine).
- Keep `min-width: 0` on flex/grid children that hold text or inputs so they can shrink.
- Avoid rigid `min-width` on controls inside narrow panels (cart, side sheets, drawers).
- Check at least a phone width (~360px), a laptop width (~1280px), and a wide desktop before finishing.
- Do not hide essential inputs (qty, rate, amount) just to fit a row; reflow instead.
